# PI-012, candidate M. Independent reading before the stored fields.
FG-M-9050e41bb6 || cls=CO mod=DEFAULT dom=PE rel=FE pol=ARC-024~ conf=M || actor=developer of caching code; act=HybridCache stays behind the contract, not named in Application contracts; trig=Application cache contract exists; scope=caching knowledge skill; exc=none; time=design; enf=text || test=Present-tense negative declarative beside a may-implement. No must, never or do not. Describes the correct shape. Behavior matches ARC-024. Not a command in form.
FG-M-f49bbb7f3e || cls=XP mod=DEFAULT dom=PE rel=NE pol=- conf=M || actor=test author; act=test repositories and EF mappings when persistence behavior is meaningful, not one per trivial Add/Get; trig=deciding persistence tests; scope=testing skill; exc=none; time=test design; enf=text || test=Contrastive not after a positive imperative. A one-test-per-trivial-method suite written to document behavior is not merely for coverage percentage, so TST-011 does not forbid it. Technique default.
FG-M-5554cb6a56 || cls=XP mod=DEFAULT dom=PE rel=NE pol=- conf=M || actor=API author; act=use 304 only for a conditional request with a still-valid cached representation; trig=304 considered; scope=http-api skill; exc=none; time=design; enf=text || test=Only-for fragment plus a descriptive is not. The claim says never, the source does not. API-003 does not cover 304. Returning 304 for a non-conditional request breaks this and no canonical policy.
FG-M-368b6c8e2a || cls=XP mod=DEFAULT dom=PE rel=NE pol=- conf=M || actor=resilience author; act=do not put validation errors, auth failures, permanent 404, business rejections in retry; trig=designing retry; scope=httpclient-factory private reference; exc=none; time=design; enf=text || test=Not retried: is a label over a classification list, not a command. RUN-016 forbids unsafe retry; retrying a validation error is safe but pointless and RUN-016 does not forbid it. Technique default.
